# Read AGENTS.md First

`AGENTS.md` at the repo root is the canonical operating guide for this business. This file only
adds what's specific to Cursor — it never restates or overrides `AGENTS.md`.

## Cursor-Specific Notes

- Scheduled sessions run headless (`cursor agent -p --sandbox enabled`). Cursor's sandbox gates the
  whole workspace, not individual paths — it cannot mark `control/**` or `state/business-state.json`
  read-only while leaving `run/`, `digests/`, and `schedule/` writable. The real protection is that
  a scheduled session's prompt asks for exactly one thing: run `core/session/run.ts` and report its
  output. Do not go further than that prompt asks, even if it looks safe to.
- Cursor's structured/JSON output mode is undocumented as of this runtime's release — do not depend
  on parsing a Cursor session's output as JSON; read it as plain text.
- This file exists because Cursor previously had no entrypoint in this repo at all. If it looks
  thin compared to `CLAUDE.md`, that is why — extend it here, not by duplicating `AGENTS.md`.
